          "The bench report requisition readiness denominator is built from the queue export, not from the dashboard total. The bench report requisition readiness definition separates a missing record in the bench availability report from a pending decision in the open requisition in the hiring plan. The measure must answer whether the bench was checked before external search. The analyst removes test records, duplicate requests, and cases outside the window, and records each removal. The talent delivery lead confirms that the remaining records belong to the same operational process. The saved query is part of the result.",
          "Every bench report requisition readiness case in the population must have a stable identifier, a start event, and an end event in the applicant tracking system. The bench report requisition readiness dictionary maps each field to the bench availability report, the placement agreement, or the open requisition in the hiring plan. The unresolved point is whether the bench was checked before external search. The analyst excludes records that cannot be tied to the open requisition in the hiring plan and reports the exclusion count. A case that starts before the window but closes inside it is counted once, with the start date noted. The population is frozen before analysis begins."
